& [JustificationIdentity] is exact
  + [justification_uuid] is b07d8199-dcf5-467f-b943-99b9a50362e3
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is bc966e32-751a-4910-ae35-d3fcd271bc56
  + [revision_source_snapshot_uuid] is 1616efd9-aad3-437a-9635-1ac9cc00ab6f
  + [status] is justified_unsigned

& [Claim] is narrow
  + one subject-local pure reconciliation of two complete output-only digest carriers is the smallest correct next dependency after supplied ordered-inventory commitment
  + the transform should establish current reproducibility and comparison scope before reporting Equal or Different
  + it should not wait for physical scanner activation because its semantics and implementation can be proven entirely over supplied bounded values

& [Support] is direct
  + the prerequisite digest carrier already retains its complete plan, assembly, ordered digest, and output-only provenance
  + Clone and immutable getters permit current complete rederivation through the already proven public transform
  + exact digest and encoding profiles prevent version ambiguity
  + exact complete TopologyScanLimits prevent comparisons under different declared capability ceilings
  + root relative path, RootDirectory kind, volume serial, and file ID prevent cross-root comparison from becoming ordinary difference
  + exact digest equality supplies a minimal Equal or Different relation without duplicating canonical encoding
  + by-value output retaining both carriers makes the decision independently inspectable

& [DependencyReason] is ordered
  + canonical sequence identity must exist before two sequences can be compared cheaply and unambiguously
  + pair reconciliation must define scope and vocabulary before future physical double-inventory code can safely reuse it
  + physical acquisition, order, completeness, and quiescence can later add provenance around this result without changing its supplied meaning
  + receipt issuance remains later because issuer, nonce, time, policy, predecessor, and physical evidence are not present

& [AlternativeA_BareDigest] is rejected
  + it is simpler computationally but disconnects result from output-only proof lineage
  + it cannot establish current rederivation, limits, root scope, or profile agreement
  + it makes evidence laundering easy and would require callers to reconstruct missing proof context

& [AlternativeB_RawAssemblies] is rejected
  + it collapses digest derivation and reconciliation into one larger authority surface
  + it adds a lower-input route and duplicate orchestration while weakening prerequisite composition
  + it obscures which side produced a current digest fault

& [AlternativeC_FullFieldDiff] is rejected
  + it duplicates the canonical sequence subject and requires another field-order and diagnostic-release contract
  + it is unnecessary for the quarantine-grade Equal or Different decision
  + naming a first difference may be mistaken for causal or temporal explanation

& [AlternativeD_PhysicalScannerFirst] is rejected for this slice
  + it requires traversal, handles, per-entry query order, completeness, Windows effects, and physical fixtures still locked
  + delaying the pure relation would leave later physical code without a signed semantic comparison boundary

& [AlternativeE_ReceiptFirst] is rejected
  + a receipt needs physical and temporal evidence plus issuer, nonce, freshness, policy, and predecessor bindings
  + supplied pair equality alone is not receipt-grade evidence

& [Counterargument] is considered
  + a caller could compare the two digest getter strings directly with one language operator
  + that operation is computationally sufficient only if the caller separately and correctly preserves complete lineage, revalidates current semantics, compares profiles, limits, and roots, and avoids temporal inflation
  + those are precisely the hard semantic duties Cantor should centralize and prove rather than repeat informally at every caller

& [Confidence] is high inside the pure boundary
  + seven independent exhaustion folds converge
  + twenty source constraints reapply without conflict
  + data identity, ownership, cardinality, transition, fault, representation, and provenance models close
  + all required operations are available in safe in-memory Rust with no dependency or effect growth
  + remaining uncertainty concerns only future physical consumers, not this supplied relation

& [Risk] is explicit
  + highest risk is rhetorical inflation of Equal into stable or quiescent physical evidence
  + next risk is scope underchecking that compares distinct roots or scan ceilings
  + next risk is current-rederivation shortcut that trusts an output string without complete present-authority reproduction
  + public vocabulary, deterministic gate order, static tests, exact scope data, and mandatory nonclaims mitigate these risks

& [InvalidationCondition] is exact
  + source, prerequisite hash, or signature drift
  + prerequisite output loses complete immutable getters, Clone, Eq, or output-only construction
  + TopologyScanLimits equality no longer represents complete declared scope
  + root strong identity semantics change
  + physical or temporal vocabulary enters the result
  + bare or lower-input overload appears
  + encoder duplication, new dependency, unsafe, platform call, effect, stale evidence, or failed proof appears

& [Decision] is proceed only through signed SJS authority
  + implement one module, export, focused tests, static boundary, evidence, and governed closure only after artifact binding and satisfaction signature
  + preserve every physical, temporal, receipt, admission, mutation, neural, distributed, FPGA, and effect boundary as absent
